  "versionNotes": [
    {
      "edition": "Current .NET runtime diagnostics boundary checked 2026-11-20",
      "items": [
        "dotnet-counters reads System.Runtime metrics through System.Diagnostics.Metrics on .NET 9 and later; .NET 8 and earlier runtimes do not expose that meter and the tool falls back to older System.Runtime EventCounters. Match tool and runtime versions.",
        "dotnet-trace collect-linux is distinct from cross-platform EventPipe collect. It requires .NET 10+, Linux x64 or Arm64, kernel 6.4+ with CONFIG_USER_EVENTS, mounted tracefs, glibc 2.27+, and root/CAP_PERFMON or CAP_SYS_ADMIN. This mode can capture native/kernel events unavailable through ordinary EventPipe collect."
      ],
      "sourceUrls": [
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/core/diagnostics/dotnet-counters",
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/core/diagnostics/dotnet-trace"
      ]
    },
    {
      "edition": "Native AOT diagnostic support page checked 2026-11-20",
      "items": [
        "Native AOT shares only some full-runtime diagnostic capabilities. The current Microsoft diagnostic support page describes EventPipe as optional via EventSourceSupport, partial runtime event support and CPU profiling, native debugging with symbols, and unsupported managed heap analysis; it specifically frames some limitations with .NET 8, so verify current runtime/version support before relying on a particular tool."
      ],
      "sourceUrls": [
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/core/deploying/native-aot/diagnostics"
      ]
    }
  ],
